. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 *
. 
.         * I run two linear OLS regression analyses with the PCA of the 5 vari
> ables for
.         * support for a more equal position of women in society (plj0621-plj0
> 625) as
.         * dependent variable and the total number of daughters as independent
>  variable,
.         * one for men and one for women.
.         * The controls are the ones listed in the PAP, with adjustments as 
.         * documented below.
.         * I then use a t test to compare coefficients of interest (on total_d
> aughters)
.         * in the men sample vs the women sample.
.         eststo men: reg pc_women total_daughters i.total_kids age2_100 loghin
> c ///
>         pgbilzeit ft_employed i.marital_stat east_germany i.migback ib3.hgnut
> s1 ///
>         i.syear if sex==1
