.         
.         * Changes from PAP:
.         * - in PAP I thought I would have a (rather) balanced panel for the 3
>  years, not a
.         * repeated cross section. Hence I pre-registered an individual fixed 
> effects
.         * OLS regression. I had to drop individual fixed effects and also the
>  clustering
.         * of standard errors at the individual level.
.         * - I calculated age differently, using syear instead of pgpiyear, si
> nce 
.         * pgpiyear was only recorded in some years.
.         * - For years of education, I used pgbilzeit instead of pgbilzt, as t
> he 
.         * second variable wasn't in SOEP Core, but in SOEP IS (misunderstandi
> ng).
.         * - For living in East/West Germany, I used sampreg instead of bgsamp
> reg, 
.         * as this was the correct variable in SOEP Core (misunderstanding).
.         * - I had to drop the control variable for being disabled, ple0040, a
> s none
.         * of the individuals with valid answers on the variables used to cons
> truct
.         * the dependent variable had been asked this question (they all had c
> ode -5).
.         * - I restricted the estimation sample to those in private households
> , with
.         * pop 1 or 2.
.         * - Unspecified in PAP: the baseline NUTS region is Berlin.
. 
.         
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS *
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics after lincom
. 
.         * (i) coefficient estimate
.         local coefficient = r(estimate)

. 
.         * (ii) standard error
.         local se = r(se)

. 
.         * (iii) family of the test statistic (t for lincom in regression cont
> ext)
.         local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.         * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom
.         local df_residual = .

.         local df_model = r(df)

. 
.         * (v) p-value
.         local p_value = 2*(1-normal(abs(r(estimate)/r(se))))

. 
.         * (vi) number of observations
.         local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.         * (vii) number of participants
.         quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.         local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.         * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.         local interpretation = "positive coefficient is in line with hypothes
> is"

. 
. 
.         * Display the saved statistics
.         di "Coefficient: `coefficient'"
Coefficient: .0162679932658325

.         di "Standard Error: `se'"
Standard Error: .0621241678757

.         di "Test Statistic Family: `test_stat_family'"
Test Statistic Family: t

.         di "Residual Degrees of Freedom: `df_residual'"
Residual Degrees of Freedom: .

.         di "Model Degrees of Freedom: `df_model'"
Model Degrees of Freedom: .

.         di "p-value: " `p_value'
p-value: .79342741

.         di "Number of observations: " `num_obs'
Number of observations: 2553

.         di "Number of participants: " `num_participants'
Number of participants: 2553

.         di "Interpretation of directionality: " "`interpretation'"
Interpretation of directionality: positive coefficient is in line with hypothes
> is

. 
.         * Export results to csv 
.         file open myfile using "$OUT/h4_results.csv", write replace
(file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived/95_re
    > sults/h4_results.csv not found)

.         file write myfile "coefficient,se,family,residual_df,model_df,p_value
> ,num_obs,num_participants,interpretation" _n

.         file write myfile "`coefficient', `se', `test_stat_family', `df_resid
> ual', `df_model',`p_value',`num_obs',`num_participants',`interpretation'" _n

.         file close myfile

. 
. 
